ty: `12`\n- Delivery date: `2026-05-16`\n- Screen size: `10.1`\n- Battery: `11 hours`\n- Rugged case: `included`\n- Warranty: `12 months`\n\n## Required deliverables\nCreate these three files under `answer/`:\n\n1. `answer/source_resolution.md`\n2. `answer/vendor_screen.md`\n3. `answer/purchase_recommendation.md`\n\nDo **not** place required deliverables in the task root.\n\n## Content required in each deliverable\n\n### `answer/source_resolution.md`\nMust include:\n- The recency rule from `requirements.md`\n- The stale Northstar CSV row dated `2026-04-24`\n- The newer Northstar update dated `2026-04-30`\n- The effective Northstar terms used for screening:\n  - unit price\n  - available quantity\n  - delivery date\n  - screen size\n  - battery rating\n  - rugged case status\n  - warranty months\n\n### `answer/vendor_screen.md`\nMust include:\n- One row/entry for **each vendor in `vendor_quotes.csv`**\n- For each vendor:\n  - effective source used\n  - eligible `yes` or `no`\n  - total cost if otherwise eligible\n  - blocking requirement when ineligible\n- Budget status for any eligible vendor\n\nVendors present:\n- Northstar\n- Atlas\n- BrightPath\n- Cobalt\n- Dockside\n\n### `answer/purchase_recommendation.md`\nMust include:\n- Selected vendor\n- Quantity\n- Unit price\n- Total cost calculation\n- Budget result\n- Delivery date\n- Short rejected-vendor summary\n\n## Process visibility requirement\nYour work must make these three checkpoints visibly separate:\n1. Source-resolution step\n2. Vendor screening step\n3. Final purchasing recommendation\n\n## Likely outcome from the provided data\nBased on the files:\n- **Northstar** is eligible using the updated 2026-04-30 terms\n- Total cost = `12 \u00d7 $178 = $2,136`\n- This is within the `$2,200` budget\n- Other vendors fail at least one hard requirement:\n  - Atlas: late delivery (`2026-05-18`)\n  - BrightPath: screen too small (`9.7`)\n  - Cobalt: battery too low (`9 hours`)\n  - Dockside: only `11` units available\